Tackles crash-consistency, non-volatile memory ordering, ABA avoidance, and safe memory reclamation in a high-concurrency data path.

## Key Concepts
- NVRAM durability and flush ordering (clwb/clflush, sfence)
- Per-slot sequence numbers to prevent ABA
- Epoch-based reclamation vs. hazard pointers
- Recovery: replay tail, prune uncommitted entries

